    "body": "`'/'` can't reach this code as higher up there is \r\n```js\r\n  if (page === '/') {\r\n    page = '/index'\r\n  }\r\n```\r\nbut, I have the feeling that that piece is a bit out of place in this function. Removing it right now causes mayhem, but might be necessary in the future to get the `/index` behavior sorted out. \r\n\r\nTo be on the safe side, in case it ever gets removed, I will use the same regex as in\r\n```js\r\npathname = pathname.replace(/(?!^)\\/$/, '')\r\n```\r\n",
